@model string
@using System.Globalization
@*
    CKEditor, from its CDN — for the admin panel (_AdminLayout) and the influencer's writer
    (Influencer/Write). Model "styles" renders the stylesheet (for <head>), "scripts" the bundle
    and, outside English, its translation. The version is pinned here and nowhere else: an upgrade
    is these URLs.

    Why the CDN and not npm: a licence key is issued for a distribution channel, and ours covers
    "cloud" — see ClientApp modules/editor.ts. A classic script runs during parsing while the page's
    bundle is a deferred module, so window.CKEDITOR is defined by the time the bundle looks for it.
    If the CDN is unreachable every editor stays a plain textarea, which still saves.

    The key (CkEditor:LicenseKey) is issued per host: Production's must cover the public host as
    well as the admin one, or the influencer writer falls back to that plain textarea.
*@
@{
    const string Cdn = "https://cdn.ckeditor.com/ckeditor5/48.4.0";
    var language = VIHouse.Business.Options.SiteCultures.Describe(CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture.Name).UrlCode;
}
@if (Model == "styles")
{
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Cdn/ckeditor5.css" crossorigin="anonymous" />
}
else
{
    <script src="@Cdn/ckeditor5.umd.js" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
    @if (language != "en")
    {
        <script src="@Cdn/translations/@(language).umd.js" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
    }
}
